  "question": {
    "text": "Two particles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> having equal charges are being accelerated through the same potential difference. Thereafter, they enter normally in a region of uniform magnetic field and describes circular paths of radii <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> respectively. The mass ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> is :",
    "image": null
  },
